From e49c24f50496843f78245e9d7edfb83f4a1a67da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:16:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] uhf: add owner: "rockchip" to satisfy this tree's
 release-branch AIDL freeze policy

Second real build failure on this module, again found by actually running
the build:

  error: hardware/rockchip/uhf/aidl/Android.bp:8:1: module
  "rockchip.uhf.aidl_interface": versions: must be set (need to be
  frozen) because: "this is a release branch - freeze it or set 'owners:'"

Traced to system/tools/aidl/build/aidl_interface.go's requireFrozenReason
check: on this tree's release config, every aidl_interface must either be
frozen (a real aidl_api/<name>/<N>/ snapshot, which the previous commit in
this series showed can't just be declared in the .bp without running
<module>-freeze-api) or declare the standard `owner:` common module
property (build/soong/android/module.go's ModuleBase.Owner(), not
something aidl-specific) to mark it as a vendor-owned interface exempt
from the platform ABI freeze requirement.

rockchip.uhf.aidl is genuinely vendor-owned, still-developing code (this
patch series' Phase 2/3 HAL boundary, not shipped anywhere yet), so
owner: "rockchip" is the correct fix, not a premature freeze. Revised the
comment block from the previous commit to document this real requirement
instead of the freeze-based plan that comment assumed before this error
was hit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 aidl/Android.bp | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/aidl/Android.bp b/aidl/Android.bp
index a618403..66259b9 100644
--- a/aidl/Android.bp
+++ b/aidl/Android.bp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 //
 aidl_interface {
     name: "rockchip.uhf.aidl",
+    owner: "rockchip",
     vendor_available: true,
     srcs: [
         "rockchip/uhf/aidl/*.aidl",
@@ -27,10 +28,16 @@ aidl_interface {
     // rockchip.hwc.proxy.aidl: that module's versions_with_info: [{version: "1", ...}] only builds
     // because its aidl_api/rockchip.hwc.proxy.aidl/1/ snapshot was actually generated by running
     // <module>-freeze-api once that interface stabilized. This interface is still mid-development
-    // (UHF-SRS-001 Phase 2/3), so it builds against "current" instead — declaring a frozen v1 here
-    // without ever running the freeze step is what breaks the build (confirmed: Soong requires the
-    // snapshot to exist on disk). The VINTF manifest/matrix fragments' <version>1</version> is still
-    // correct as-is: an unfrozen "current" AIDL interface is conventionally treated as version 1
-    // for VINTF matching purposes until it is actually frozen (`m rockchip.uhf.aidl-freeze-api`),
-    // at which point that freeze becomes version 1 for real and this comment should be removed.
+    // (UHF-SRS-001 Phase 2/3) and builds against "current" instead.
+    //
+    // This tree's release config (system/tools/aidl/build/aidl_interface.go's requireFrozenReason
+    // check) refuses to build any unfrozen aidl_interface unless it declares owner: - confirmed by
+    // actually hitting that PropertyErrorf, not by inspection. owner: "rockchip" is the correct,
+    // real escape hatch for a vendor-owned interface that isn't part of the frozen platform ABI
+    // (see build/soong/android/module.go's Owner()/commonProperties.Owner - a standard property,
+    // not something specific to aidl_interface). Once this interface actually stabilizes for a
+    // release, replace owner: with a real `m rockchip.uhf.aidl-freeze-api` snapshot instead.
+    // The VINTF manifest/matrix fragments' <version>1</version> needs no change either way: an
+    // unfrozen "current" AIDL interface is conventionally treated as version 1 for VINTF matching
+    // until it is actually frozen.
 }
